  "description": "At Reid we have sustainability at heart. We want to make sure people have the choice of a more environmentally friendly method of transport at an accessible price point. The KADe truly embodies that mantra. We plant a tree for every product we sell, but we also aim to plant the seed of sustainable transport for generations to come.\nThe KADe was the result of over 2 years of R&D with extensive testing. The design was finalised to give as much load carrying capacity whilst retaining a smooth and controlled ride. We chose 24” wheels paired with reinforced 3.0” tyres to both improve ride quality and grip whilst keeping the centre of gravity as low as possible.\nThe step through frame with relaxed seat tube angle paired to a fully adjustable stem gives a huge range of rider height variance. It’s as close as you can get to a one size fits all situation fitting riders between 5’4” and 6’4”. The KADE comes equipped with dual 48v batteries with a combined 21.6ah storage. These feed the mid drive Ananda M100 motor that has an impressive 110nm of torque. Enough power to get any load moving and keep it moving for hours!\nSpeaking of loads, the choice of what you carry is up to you! With a max load capacity of 100kg on the rear rack and 20kg on the front*, built in automatic front and rear lights, and plenty of accessories the KADe has true versatility. The school run? The weekly shop? The trip to the beach? Or even use the KADe as a delivery vehicle. It will handle them all. Obviously with the extra demand of cargo comes the extra demand on the bikes components. We have equipped the KADe with 9 speed Shimano Altus shifting and Shimano MT200 hydraulic disc brakes that you can always count on.\nThe KADe is a big hit with our team and their families, we’re sure you’ll find the same.\nComplete with mudguards, rear carrier rack and front rack, other add ons are optional.\n*No passengers should sit on the rear rack without the optional padded seat and wheel guards.\n*Total mass not to exceed 200kg, including the bike.",
